Copied modules: src/steam/accounts.js, game-auth.js, store.js and errors.js.
The original account manager and ticket-lease interface are retained. This
project supplies a smaller features adapter and a new AdminLogger controller.
No account store, passwords, saved login tokens or historical accounts were copied.

plugin/AdminLogger.cs is a modified copy of the user-provided integration target,
attributed in its metadata to 1AK1 (original Admin Logger 2.5.5; local revision
2.5.6). The integration fixes are reproducible with scripts/prepare-plugin.mjs.
Its separate licensing status is
not established by this project's upstream Apache license.

src/network/china-ipv4.json contains an IPv4 prefix snapshot from
https://github.com/gaoyifan/china-operator-ip (ip-lists branch, china.txt),
Copyright (c) 2017 Yifan Gao, MIT License.
The full license is included in docs/china-operator-ip-LICENSE.txt.
Snapshot source, retrieval time and upstream SHA256 are recorded in the JSON.
Refresh with: node scripts/update-china-ipv4.mjs

src/steam/webapi-ticket.js independently implements the WebAPI ticket wire
layout documented by Steamworks and described in SteamRE/SteamKit's
SteamAuthTicket.GetAuthTicketForWebApi (TicketType 5, service identity,
ownership-ticket framing and WebAPI buffer padding). Reference:
https://github.com/SteamRE/SteamKit/blob/master/SteamKit2/SteamKit2/Steam/Handlers/SteamAuthTicket/SteamAuthTicket.cs
It uses the existing, pinned steam-user 5.3.0 connection. No SteamKit library
or copied SteamKit source is distributed in this project.

src/facepunch/client-config.json records the telemetry endpoint with an empty
application-key value. The public repository does not distribute that key;
set FACEPUNCH_API_KEY in the runtime environment for telemetry research.
Each upload additionally requires its own account's Steam-issued WebAPI ticket.
The performance schema was observed locally; the included hardware, session,
input and performance values are generated simulation data, not recorded users.
